    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3450" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκρ-έσπερος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>on edge of evening</i> (
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄκρος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11
				</span></i>
			), hence, <i>at nightfall</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Th.</u>
				25
			</span></i> (cf. Sch.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				7.633
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Crin.
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν ἀκρέσπερον [νύκτα</span>]
				<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				619b21
			</span></i>, as cited by <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				8.353b
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρχέσπερον</span> codd. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
			</span></i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄχρις ἑσπερίου</span> codf. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
			</span></i>):—neut. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκρέσπερον</span> as Adv., <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				24.77
			</span></i>; but, <i>on approach of evening</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Epid.</u>
				7.23
			</span></i>.</div>
